    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d627">

                <pb facs="0663" n="651" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg651"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/8–2545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Fullerton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-29T20:00:00-04:00">August 29, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4093. For Villard. Urtel 5153 Aug. 25, 2 p.m.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d627-f1"/>
                    Importance of having radiotelegraph station in Tangier as a relay point to
                    Eastern Europe, Near East and Far East cannot be too greatly emphasized and
                    right of US interests to establish such a station must, under no circumstances,
                    be jeopardized. However there is obviously no objection to technical control of
                    such stations such as that exercised by FCC<anchor n="80" xml:id="d627-f2"/> in
                    this country.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
